      "heading": "Quick Answer",
      "body": "Quick Answer\n\nThe Tunnel Escape Fates Entwined languages on Steam are listed in the Supported Languages table for AppID 4285110. English ships with interface text, full audio, and subtitles. Traditional Chinese ships with interface text only. No other interface, audio, or subtitle languages are confirmed as of 2026-09-30.\n\nTunnel Escape Fates Entwined languages: English (interface + full audio + subtitles)\n\nThe Steam store Supported Languages table for AppID 4285110 marks English as supported across all three columns: interface, full audio, and subtitles. The Full Audio tag on the Steam row means the game ships with English voice acting or voiced cinematics; the Subtitles tag means English captions can be turned on in-game.\n\nThis is the only locale the store currently ships with full audio and subtitles. The English row is the canonical local play option for the launch build and is the fallback language for buyers whose Steam client is set to a locale the store does not yet support.\n\nHow Steam handles the English fallback\n\nWhen a buyer's Steam client language is not on the Supported Languages table, Steam falls back to the first language marked Full Audio on the store row. For Tunnel Escape Fates Entwined that fallback is English. The fallback applies to in-game text, voice lines, and caption rendering for buyers outside the supported locale set.\n\nTraditional Chinese (interface only)\n\nThe Steam store table also lists Traditional Chinese, but only with the Interface column populated. Traditional Chinese is not marked Full Audio or Subtitles on the store row, so it should be read as a UI-text translation rather than a full localization.\n\nIn practice this means:\n\n- In-game menus, settings labels, and Steam overlay text render in Traditional Chinese for buyers whose Steam client or game language is set to zh-Hant.\n- Voice lines, cutscene audio, and on-screen captions stay in English.\n\nIf you need Traditional Chinese subtitles or full audio, that is not announced as of 2026-09-30.\n\nOther interface, audio, and subtitle languages\n\nNot announced as of 2026-09-30. The Steam store Supported Languages table does not mark any other interface, audio, or subtitle column as supported. Common storefront locales that are not on the table include Simplified Chinese, Japanese, Korean, French, German, Spanish, Italian, Portuguese, Russian, Polish, Dutch, Turkish, Arabic, and the Nordic languages. Each additional locale would change the answer if Elzee or Saikey Studios publishes a Steam news update, a Steam store row, or a patch note that adds a new language to the table.\n\nWhat the Supported Languages columns mean\n\nThe Steam store Supported Languages table uses three columns: Interface, Full Audio, and Subtitles. The Interface column tells you whether the on-screen menus and settings text are translated. The Full Audio column tells you whether the game ships with that language's voice acting. The Subtitles column tells you whether that language's captions can be turned on for spoken audio. A row marked Interface only means menus are translated but spoken audio and captions stay in another language (English for the Traditional Chinese row)."
